

   =====( PageDoor V0.76 )============================================


           Trion PageDoor CliDoor.

           (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '96-'97. All rights reserved.

           Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


        This is a Sysop Page Door ... when a user enters it it will
        tell the user if the sysop is in.
        If the sysop is around the User can give a chat reason.
        If the sysop is not around the door will ask if he wants to
        leave a chat reason anyway.
        A chat reason is valid if there are at least 5 characters.
        If a user just taps enter this question is not much use
        to the sysop.
        The reason will be written to the log of the BBS node.

        After this the door will play the page sample 4 times.
        While doing this a window will pop up on the workbench screen
        with the chat reason and the User name/node.
        Also the workbench screen will come to front.

        Also on this window there are 4 buttons for DeIconize, Normal
        chat, LineChat and SplitChat.
        If any of these are clicked .. during the samples the BBS screen
        will be DeIconized And/Or come to front.
        If one of the normal chat/linechat/splitchat buttons is clicked
        a chatter will also be started.

        To Use this door place something like this in your menu file:


Cmd "P" , 0-255
   CliDoor  "doors:chatdoor/PageDoor ~50 "
EndCmd


        If you want to be able to start the chatters from the 
        workbench window there has to be 3 entries in the SAME menu
        as the PageCommand is with a "-" a "=" and a "\" cmd.
        After these commands you can start the chat mode you would
        like to pop up with this command.
        You will probably add something like this:


Cmd "-" , 0-255
   CliDoor  "doors:chatdoor/LineChat ~50 "
EndCmd

Cmd "=" , 0-255
   CliDoor  "doors:chatdoor/SplitChat ~50 "
EndCmd

Cmd "\" , 0-255 , S
   ClrScr
   FlushBuffer                           ; Flush the return after "\"
   PushIntoBuffer "Hallo daar !!|"
   StartChat
EndCmd


        Note that after the "\" command there is a 'S' flag, this means
        that the chat mode can't be started remote.
        This is done because a user can't get out of the chat mode
        without help from the sysop.
        So if he accidently presses the \ he has to hangup.
        You could also add the 'S' flag to the commands for the
        chatdoors so only the sysop can start them .. but on the
        other hand .. it can be usefull if a co-sysop wants to
        show you something that he can start and stop the chatter.


        Note that the "-" and "=" characters are choosen for a special
        reason .. the "=" symbolises the 2 windows of the splitchat
        door and the "-" symbolises the window of the linechat door.
        This makes it easier to remember wich key to use to startup
        a chat door.

